# Hand-written redirect rules.
#
# This file is the human-edited half of the site's redirects. At build time
# scripts/create-worker-entry.mjs merges it with the part-page dedup map and
# writes the combined list to dist/_redirects, which is the single file
# Cloudflare actually reads.
#
# Syntax:   <from>  <to>  <status>       (one rule per line, whitespace-separated)
#   - paths only: `_redirects` cannot match scheme or hostname, so http:// and
#     www. collapsing is configured in the Cloudflare dashboard instead.
#   - rules are evaluated top-down and the FIRST match wins; a duplicate source
#     path would silently shadow every rule below it.
#   - `#` starts a comment; blank lines are ignored.
#   - Cloudflare only honours 301, 302, 303, 307, 308 and 200 (rewrite).
#     410 Gone is NOT supported here and would be silently ignored.
#     Retired URLs that must answer 410 live in src/data/retired-urls.txt and
#     are served by dist/_worker.js/index.js instead. Do not add 410 rules to
#     this file - the build strips them and warns.
#
# Sections:
#   A. legacy marketing URLs -> their current home
#   B. the retired engine-family.com category tree -> surviving brand hubs
#      (one-time migration, 2026-10-10; every target verified to exist)
#   C. retired imported shells -> the page that genuinely replaces them

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
